BT /F1 13 Tf 72 750 Td 15 TL (4. Worked check - half-up calibration example) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 728 Td 12 TL
(Worked example matching the proto_estimators check. Species counts at one site are {A: 5, B:) Tj T*
(3, C: 1, D: 1}. Then n = 10, S = 4, and p = \(0.5, 0.3, 0.1, 0.1\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(H = -\(0.5*ln 0.5 + 0.3*ln 0.3 + 0.1*ln 0.1 + 0.1*ln 0.1\) = 1.1683.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(D = 1 - \(0.5^2 + 0.3^2 + 0.1^2 + 0.1^2\) = 1 - 0.36 = 0.6400.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Here f1 = 2 \(species C and D\) and f2 = 0 \(no species has count 2\). Chao bias-corrected = 4 +) Tj T*
(2*\(2-1\)/\(2*\(0+1\)\) = 4 + 2/2 = 5.0000.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(So the expected row for these counts is n = 10, S = 4, H = 1.1683, D = 0.6400, ChaoBC =) Tj T*
(5.0000. Any implementation that reproduces these four values on these counts has the) Tj T*
(formulas, the natural log, the Gini-Simpson form, and the bias-corrected Chao form right.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
endstream
